--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The timetable solver in `solver.py` is a Python port of the constraint solver
from Chronos (github.com/samprith02/chronos-teacher-erp-timetable), by the same
author, and is relicensed here under Apache 2.0. The port is not a
transliteration: it adds multi-period lab blocks, per-semester day lengths,
scope pinning, conflict-directed backtracking and a stuck-variable cap, and it
fixes a search oscillation present in the original. `solver.py`'s module
docstring records what changed and why.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project depends on two third-party packages, both permissively licensed,
neither vendored into this repository:

    FastAPI    MIT License        https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi
    Uvicorn    BSD 3-Clause       https://github.com/encode/uvicorn

Everything else is the Python standard library. There is no LLM SDK — `llm.py`
speaks OpenAI-compatible HTTP over `urllib` directly. The web console in
`static/index.html` loads no external scripts, styles, fonts or images; it is a
single self-contained file.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All data in this project is SYNTHETIC and generated by `db.py`. The institution
("Vidyatech Institute", vidyatech.edu.in), its departments, faculty, students,
USNs, phone numbers, email addresses, timetable, leave records and placement
statistics are invented. They are modelled on the structure of an Indian
autonomous/VTU-affiliated engineering college, but no real institution, person
or record is represented.

No third-party dataset is redistributed here.

Faculty and student phone numbers are random 10-digit strings and are not
verified against any numbering plan. They are filler for UI layout and must not
be dialled or treated as contactable.
